A||||10||Dan010||idle rpm||||1||
Z||000000||Dan010||10-23-2001||08:00 AM||||What is the correct rpm for a 86 2.8 (auto)at idle?<BR>Last night I checked it and it was 1500 and went as high as 1800 and after 5 min. or so, never droped below 1300.<BR>Would like to set this correctly before checking timing. Thanks<BR>I know there is the sencor to control this, not sure it is working correctly.||||reg||1
Z||000001||87GTZ34||10-23-2001||09:15 AM||||When warmed up, 900 +/- 50.  It sounds like you have a vacuum leak which typically is the EGR tube or valve. I would start with an inspection of those two first as they are most common.  Did this symptom start all of the sudden?||||reg||1
Z||000002||Dan010||10-23-2001||10:27 AM||||No, Bought this car about a month ago, been this way, did have a code and found a vac. leak to map, fixed this and no more codes,<BR>but thought it could still be more leaks,<BR>car runs fairly good, but has a stumble on takeoff, not bad, but think it could run better.<BR>This is a toy/hobbie auto, so am enjoying this forum and all the info.<BR>I am slowly checking this and that.<BR>Thanks for your thoughts!!!!!||||reg||1
Z||000003||88CoupeV6||10-23-2001||10:53 AM||||Welcome to the forum. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>I would check the EGR tube. They tend to crack and cause the idle to go up. The idle is controlled by the ECM and is non-adjustable. Only thing would be a vacuum leak or the IAC(Idle Air Control)valve.<P>When you check the timing you must ground the ECM connector in the center console. It is next to the lighter behind the black cover.<P>Good luck and please keep us posted<P>------------------<BR>Josh<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/newsig.jpg">    <BR>:D  <BR><A HREF="http://albums.photopoint.com/j/AlbumList?u=1249362" TARGET=_blank>My pics</A>||||reg||7
Z||000004||btoth||10-23-2001||02:24 PM||||If you're concerned about other leaks in the little vacuum lines, Rodney's steel vacuum lines would be a good investment.<P>My auto is at 900~800 in Drive, about 1000 RPMs in Park when warmed up.  When cold it runs about 500 RPMs higher than normal.<P>When my EGR valve went bad it didn't change anything but set off a code at highway speeds.  The ERG tube could be a possibilty, I haven't had mine crack though.  Was the code you found the actual MAP sensor or just a vacuum leak?  If it was the MAP sensor, replace it with an ACDelco replacement... the MAP controls a bunch of stuff.<P>[EDIT]<P>The idle is adjustable, some little screw hidden somewhere, but you should never have to touch it.  If you're idle is off, it is most likely a leak or timming/ignition problems.<p>[This message has been edited by btoth (edited 10-23-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||Dan010||10-23-2001||05:02 PM||||the leak was the vacuum line to the map,<BR>coming from the steel line on the fire wall.<BR>haven't had a code since<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000006||Dan010||10-25-2001||08:01 AM||||Well, last night tried the carb cleaner spray<BR>onb vacuum lines and egr tube, no change in idle speed at all. Then tried Joe Tormas test for the IAC, did as instructed, the engine would not idle at all, would stall, hooked everything back together, drove it over 35 for a time, and the idle is back to 1200 to 1300, did not drill out and adjust idle screw.<BR>What would be your suggestions??<BR>Very tempted to not worry about this, it just bangs a little harder than it should when putting it into gear (auto). Need to change mounts maybe Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000007||Philphine||10-25-2001||11:01 AM||||i just got an 86gt that had a vaccume leak in the egr tube but it was under the insulation so when i sprayed carb cleaner i had to fog the whole area just to get a little reaction. i ended up getting a new can to get the straw that goes with it. then i could stick the straw into the insulation and got a better reaction to it.||||reg||1
Z||000008||btoth||10-25-2001||11:05 AM||||How many miles on the car?<P>Did you check the timming by putting a paper clip in the A and B holes of the diagnostic terminal under the cig lighter?  The timming should be at the 10 degree mark.||||reg||1
